# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The server is compiled to a real .exe in-tree, and a .syso produced by
# rsrc/goversioninfo is architecture- and toolchain-specific. Neither belongs in
# history: the .syso in particular is regenerated by the documented build step,
# so committing it would make every other checkout fail to link on a different
# Go/Windows combination.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.syso
server/smart-remote-app.exe
server/smart-remote-test.exe

# Flutter / Dart
mobile/build/
mobile/.dart_tool/
mobile/.flutter-plugins
mobile/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
mobile/.packages
mobile/pubspec.lock
mobile/**/generated_plugin_registrant.dart
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/local.properties
mobile/android/app/debug/
mobile/android/app/profile/
mobile/android/app/release/
mobile/ios/Pods/
mobile/ios/.symlinks/
mobile/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
mobile/ios/Flutter/Flutter.podspec
mobile/ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
mobile/ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh
mobile/macos/Pods/
mobile/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
mobile/linux/flutter/ephemeral/

# Go
server/vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The server writes its own log next to the binary. It is machine-specific and
# can grow without bound, and it records the pairing PIN in plain text, so it
# must never be committed.
*.log
config/macros.json

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Release artefacts. These are copied out of mobile/build after a release build
# so they are easy to find and sideload, but a 50MB APK per commit bloats the
# history without adding anything a rebuild cannot reproduce.
release.apk
server/smart-remote-app.exe
server/smart-remote-test.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal scratch files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are local notes kept by hand, not build output. They are ignored
# explicitly by name so a broad cleanup glob can never sweep them up.
_f.txt
_flutter.txt
server/_s.txt
mobile/_analyze.txt

# Transient output written by the icon and build tooling while inspecting
# intermediate results. Matched as a group so a new one never has to be
# registered here by hand.
#
# No "!" exemption is needed for the notes above: they are already ignored on
# their own lines, and a "!" line would un-ignore them - the opposite of what is
# wanted. The glob sits below them for exactly that ordering reason.
_[a-zA-Z0-9]*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local design material (never committed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "assets-smart remote/" holds the logo SOURCES (kept) alongside bulky local
# material: screenshots, exported site drafts and notes (~10MB). Only the
# logo sources under description_picture/logo-svg/ and logo-new/ belong in
# history; the rest would bloat every clone for zero build value.
assets-smart remote/description_picture/app-pcturese/
assets-smart remote/description_picture/server-pictures/
assets-smart remote/description_picture/smart-remote-info.jpg
assets-smart remote/site-by claude/
assets-smart remote/smart-remote-logo.svg
assets-smart remote/totch final.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test / coverage artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
*.coverprofile

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Task scratch capture output (temporary logs and screenshots)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captured command/test/analyze output and phone screenshots land in the repo
# root while working; they are throwaway and must never be committed.
bld.txt
devinfo.txt
pair_shot*.png
analyze_*.txt
test_*.txt
diff_*.txt
mutant_*.txt
status_*.txt

# Captured release-inspection output (version/signature/asset dumps).
# Listed by explicit name only - a broad "*.txt" would also hide the tracked
# documentation and per-file scratch notes above.
apkver*.txt
check*.txt
ghrel*.txt
gitdiff*.txt
relbuild*.txt
sig*.txt
ver_*.txt
